  <h2>What the evidence does—and does not—show</h2>
  <p>Australian purchaser comments at The Good Guys describe useful reheating, baking and roasting versatility. Some reviewers are still learning the functions, and the retailer says reviews may be incentivised. Those reports help identify ownership considerations; they do not prove long-term reliability or performance in your kitchen.</p>
  <p>Rachel Ogden's firsthand Tech Advisor review of the UK NN-CD88 family found a large footprint, a learning curve and variable crisping results. That supports caution about transferring air-fryer recipes unchanged. It is not a test of the exact Australian suffix, and we have used the Australian manual—not the review's cooking setup—for accessory and installation instructions.</p>
  <p>AHC has not cooked with this model. Our confidence is moderate. We checked Australian specifications, the manual, warranty and support information, owner feedback, the recall register and the exact retailer offer on 14 October 2026. The Good Guys displayed delivery to a Brisbane 4000 test postcode and local stock; this does not establish nationwide stock or a future delivery promise. Panasonic lists a 12-month small-appliance manufacturer warranty; read its terms and keep proof of purchase.</p>

  <h2>Before you order</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>List three meals you cook often and whether their parts need to cook simultaneously.</li>
    <li>Measure the appliance, operating clearances, open door and your largest suitable dish.</li>
    <li>Check the actual air-fry controls, included accessories and storage space.</li>
    <li>Read the cookware and cleaning instructions before assuming existing containers will work.</li>
    <li>Confirm the Australian model, delivery, returns and support route with the retailer.</li>
  </ol>

